course: dictionary
lesson: 3836
title: Fortify: stronger in three ways
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning with the words around them. Fortify is one of these. «Legionaries built a fortified camp every night.» The word built is your clue: a camp was made stronger, with walls and ditches to keep enemies out.
explain: «Milk, cheese, yoghurt and fortified foods all contain calcium.» The brackets explain it: fortified foods have extra vitamins or minerals added. So to fortify food means to add goodness to it.
explain: A hero can fortify himself with a cup of tea, which makes him stronger or braver. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: To fortify means to make something stronger.
fact: To fortify a place means to protect it with walls, towers or ditches.
fact: To fortify food means to add extra vitamins or minerals to it, as in «fortified cereal».
fact: To fortify yourself means to make yourself stronger or braver, for example with food, a drink or encouragement.
fact: «Fortified» is the past tense, and «fortifying» is the -ing form.
exercise: «Legionaries built a fortified camp every night.» What does fortified mean here? | Left empty for the night | Painted in bright colours | Full of hot food | *Made stronger with walls and ditches
exercise: «Fortified foods» have extra vitamins or minerals added. What does fortified mean in this phrase? | Foods that are hard and dry | Foods from a castle | *Foods with extra vitamins or minerals added | Foods cooked for a very long time
exercise: «He fortified himself with a cup of tea.» What does fortified himself suggest? | Became angry with the tea | Fell asleep on the sofa | Felt tired and sad | *Made himself stronger or braver
test: The town was ___ with high walls and towers to keep enemies out. Which word fits? | fortune | fortifies | *fortified | fortify
test: «The cereal is ___ with iron and vitamins.» Which word fits? | *fortified | fortify | fortifies | fortress
exam: The hill fort was ___ with a deep ditch and a wooden wall, so the enemy could not get in easily. Which word fits best? | fortifies | fortify | fortune | *fortified
